 \"observations\": {\n          \"text\": \"[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"O1\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"The static, pooled and target-aware references have AUC 0.6050036145, 0.6102261137 and 0.6133619861. Pooling and target conditioning each improve both overall metrics at seed 42. Ordinary round-one controls exactly reproduce the corresponding reported reference metrics and slices.\\\",\\\"evidence_refs\\\":[\\\"baseline-static\\\",\\\"baseline-pooled\\\",\\\"baseline-din\\\",\\\"r0001-ordinary_pool\\\",\\\"r0001-ordinary_din\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"O2\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"All nine supplied trials succeeded operationally, including both latest arms. Full correction is a negative performance trajectory, not a failed execution: AUC falls by 0.0017334134 for pooling and 0.0001905060 for DIN, with worse Logloss in both. No failed execution receipt or additional abandoned branch is supplied.\\\",\\\"evidence_refs\\\":[\\\"baseline-static\\\",\\\"baseline-pooled\\\",\\\"baseline-din\\\",\\\"r0001-ordinary_pool\\\",\\\"r0001-count_corrected_pool\\\",\\\"r0001-ordinary\",\n          \"truncated\": true\n        },\n        \"interpretations\": {\n          \"text\": \"[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"I1\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Partial correction may trade useful behavior intensity against multiplicity in pooling, where full balancing overcorrects. The same primary-objective explanation is unsupported for DIN at seed 42.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"provisional; local controlled pooling signal, negative DIN evidence\\\",\\\"evidence_refs\\\":[\\\"r0001-ordinary_pool\\\",\\\"r0001-count_corrected_pool\\\",\\\"r0002-half_pool\\\",\\\"r0001-ordinary_din\\\",\\\"r0001-count_corrected_din\\\",\\\"r0002-half_din\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"I2\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Learned target-aware retrieval may reduce sensitivity to the explicit normalization strength, but the sign reversal of the interaction weakens a general claim that attention compensates beneficially for correction. Optimization, embedding geometry and score adaptation remain alternatives.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"hypothesis; no identified c\",\n          \"truncated\": true\n        },\n        \"alternatives\": {\n          \"text\": \"[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"A1\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Seed-specific optimization could explain the small DIN gaps and the half-pooling gain.\\\",\\\"discriminating_evidence\\\":\\\"Paired seeds 43 and 44 under the existing recipe, with frozen arms; report every paired difference and mean/range. User-cluster bootstrap requires an authorized host interface and predictions/identities that are not currently available.\\\",\\\"evidence_refs\\\":[\\\"r0002-half_pool\\\",\\\"r0002-half_din\\\",\\\"r0001-ordinary_pool\\\",\\\"r0001-ordinary_din\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"A2\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Visible type counts convey useful reliability/intensity, and rare actions can be noisy rather tha\",\n          \"truncated\": true\n        },\n        \"falsifiers\": {\n          \"text\": \"[{\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Half strength rescues the full-correction DIN AUC penalty.\\\",\\\"observed_evidence\\\":\\\"Half DIN is below both ordinary and full DIN on AUC.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"Contradicted at seed 42; repetition needed for generalization.\\\",\\\"evidence_refs\\\":[\\\"r0002-half_din\\\",\\\"r0001-ordinary_din\\\",\\\"r0001-count_corrected_din\\\"]},{\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Reducing frequent-type mass necessarily improves prediction.\\\",\\\"observed_evidence\\\":\\\"Mass changes are active at both strengths, yet full correction hurts both branches and half correction hurts DIN.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"Unsupported as a general explanation; activity is insufficient.\\\",\\\"evidence_re\",\n          \"truncated\": true\n        },\n        \"limitations\": {\n          \"text\": \"[\\\"Only seed 42 is measured. Aggregate summaries cannot yield paired user-cluster confidence intervals; identical bridge metrics do not supply independent repetitions.\\\",\\\"The supplied diagnostics are candidate-authored, first-512 ordered impressions and not independently verified. Four empty and 40 single-type cases provide limited invariance checks.\\\",\\\"Attention masses, score means and summary L2 changes do not establish event relevance, causal importance or performance mediation. Cross-checkpoint changes conflate retraining and normalization.\\\",\\\"All slice analysis is exploratory. Counts are supplied in the complete slice table. No invented sufficiency threshold is imposed; empty-history (310 positives), pv-absent (397) and frequency-1_2 (1045) slices need particular caution. Positive exposur\",\n          \"truncated\": true\n        },\n        \"next_action\": {\n          \"text\": \"{\\\"action\\\":\\\"Retain baseline-din. In a later authorized experiment phase, complete a bounded paired-seed study of the existing arms; do not edit models, train, request test feedback or freeze a final suite during this analysis.\\\",\\\"observation\\\":\\\"Half strength improves pooling but does not recover the DIN AUC penalty; the correction interaction changes sign across strengths.\\\",\\\"mechanism_hypothesis\\\":\\\"Partial normalization may retain useful intensity in pooling; target-aware retrieval is less sensitive to normalization, or the apparent differences are seed-specific optimization effects. A repeat can discriminate reproducible performance from seed variation, but does not alone identify a mechanism.\\\",\\\"nearest_existing_work\\\":\\\"The six existing normalization arms are the immediate comparison suite. This is repetition and attribution, not a new contribution; inspect primary normalization literature b\",\n          \"truncated\": true\n        },\n        \"decision\": {\n          \"text\": \"{\\\"incumbent\\\":\\\"baseline-din\\\",\\\"promote_latest_candidate\\\":false,\\\"research_status\\\":\\\"Retain ordinary DIN. Half pooling is a preliminary within-pooling improvement; half and full DIN are negative primary-objective results. Complete bounded replication before mechanism or selection claims; do not broaden coefficient tuning.\\\",\\\"scientific_maturity\\\":\\\"Single-seed controlled local observations; neither repeated support nor statistical significance established.\\\"}\",\n          \"truncated\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"proposed_updates\": [\n        {\n          \"statement\": {\n            \"text\": \"The prior half-strength rescue hypothesis has branch-dependent evidence: half pooling beats both pooling endpoints, while half DIN fails to recover full-DIN AUC and trails ordinary DIN. Preserve the original hypothesis and this qualification together.\",\n            \"truncated\": false\n          },\n          \"evidence_refs\": [\n            \"r0002-half_pool\",\n            \"r0002-half_din\",\n            \"r0001-ordinary_pool\",\n            \"r0001-count_corrected_pool\",\n            \"r0001-ordinary_din\",\n            \"r0001-count_corrected_din\"\n          ],\n          \"source_maturity\": \"local_observation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": {\n            \"text\": \"The full-strength positive AUC interaction reverses at half strength. A general positive compensation interpretation is weakened; DIN flatness, optimization and seed variation remain competing explanations.\",\n            \"truncated\": false\n          },\n          \"evidence_refs\": [\n            \"r0001-ordinary_pool\",\n            \"r0001-count_corrected_pool\",\n            \"r0001-ordinary_din\",\n            \"r0001-count_corrected_din\",\n            \"r0002-half_pool\",\n            \"r0002-half_din\"\n          ],\n          \"source_maturity\": \"hypothesis\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": {\n            \"text\": \"Half DIN reverses the full-strength category-absent AUC gain and still worsens Logloss. No stable subgroup mechanism or gate is supported.\",\n            \"truncated\": false\n          },\n          \"evidence_refs\": [\n            \"r0001-ordinary_din\",\n            \"r0001-count_corrected_din\",\n            \"r0002-half_din\"\n          ],\n          \"source_maturity\": \"local_observation\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_trial_refs\": [\n        \"baseline-static\",\n        \"baseline-pooled\",\n        \"baseline-din\",\n        \"r0001-ordinary_pool\",\n        \"r0001-count_corrected_pool\",\n        \"r0001-ordinary_din\",\n        \"r0001-count_corrected_din\",\n        \"r0002-half_pool\",\n        \"r0002-half_din\"\n      ],\n      \"full_ref\": \"memory://agent-r0002\",\n      \"full_sha256\": \"8a8a29b6e47bca12ce85994e80282fea9aac8858a7595941c022b9d8592fb729\",\n      \"summary_notice\": \"Bounded index view, not complete evidence. Read full_ref for original observations, alternatives and limitations. No maturity promotion is implied.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"agent-r0001\",\n      \"knowledge_type\": \"agent\",\n      \"maturity\": \"hypothesis\",\n      \"task_scope\": \"bd5ca20f6c2ca3e084ad11e12bf6200adbd293e060e1efb96dcb070f64ff81fa\",\n      \"protocol_hash\": \"9c1635366a72f4c4f67708ee7ae9b72a1b90197ffed3485736388ceff7c91d3e\",\n      \"summary\": {\n        \"observations\": {\n          \"text\": \"[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"O1\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"History pooling improves AUC over static features by 0.0052224992242449, and target-aware attention improves over pooling by 0.0031358724110028. Both changes also lower overall Logloss. History and target conditioning therefore have local predictive value under this recipe.\\\",\\\"evidence_refs\\\":[\\\"baseline-static\\\",\\\"baseline-pooled\\\",\\\"baseline-din\\\"],\\\"maturity\\\":\\\"local_observation\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"O2\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"Both ordinary arms reproduce their corresponding ancestors exactly in aggregate AUC, Logloss, and every reported slice metric, at identical parameter counts. This supports use of the ordinary arms as bridges for intervention attribution.\\\",\\\"evidence_refs\\\":[\\\"baseline-pooled\\\",\\\"baseline-din\\\",\\\"r0001-ordinary_pool\\\",\\\"r0001-ordinary_din\\\"],\\\"maturity\\\":\\\"controlled_support_within_seed\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"O3\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"Full count correction lowers AUC and raises Logloss in both branches. Th\",\n          \"truncated\": true\n        },\n        \"interpretations\": {\n          \"text\": \"[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"I1\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Behavior multiplicity can dominate the normalization without being a harmful bias. Removing multiplicity changed summaries and hurt overall prediction in this setting.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"provisional explanation; full-correction benefit unsupported\\\",\\\"evidence_refs\\\":[\\\"r0001-ordinary_pool\\\",\\\"r0001-count_corrected_pool\\\",\\\"r0001-ordinary_din\\\",\\\"r0001-count_corrected_din\\\"],\\\"alternatives\\\":[\\\"Useful intensity or composition information was removed from the aggregate.\\\",\\\"Rare actions were upweighted despite weak or noisy target relevance.\\\",\\\"Optimization and representation scaling changed.\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"I2\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Learned target-aware scores may compensate for, or be less sensitive to, the imposed count correction. The smaller DIN penalty and higher uncorrected pv mass in the corrected-trained\",\n          \"truncated\": true\n        },\n        \"alternatives\": {\n          \"text\": \"[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"A1\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Sampling and initialization variation could reverse the small DIN difference.\\\",\\\"discriminating_evidence\\\":\\\"Paired seeds 43 and 44 for ordinary, partial and full corrected DIN; paired user-cluster intervals only if the host authorizes access to the necessary identities/predictions.\\\",\\\"evidence_refs\\\":[\\\"r0001-ordinary_din\\\",\\\"r0001-count_corrected_din\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"A2\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Total visible count is a useful reliability or behavior-intensity cue, rather than purely unwanted multiplicity.\\\",\\\"discriminating_evidence\\\":\\\"A predeclared partial-count correction tests overcorrect\",\n          \"truncated\": true\n        },\n        \"falsifiers\": {\n          \"text\": \"[{\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Full correction improves the primary objective.\\\",\\\"observed_evidence\\\":\\\"Both paired branches have lower AUC and higher Logloss.\\\",\\\"current_status\\\":\\\"Contradicted for the supplied seed/recipe, not a universal refutation.\\\",\\\"evidence_refs\\\":[\\\"r0001-ordinary_pool\\\",\\\"r0001-count_corrected_pool\\\",\\\"r0001-ordinary_din\\\",\\\"r0001-count_corrected_din\\\"]},{\\\"claim\\\":\\\"The candidate failed because correction was numerically inactive.\\\",\\\"observed_evidence\\\":\\\"Same-checkpoint mass and summary changes are large on mixed histories, with zero padding mass and near-normalized weights.\\\",\\\"current_status\\\":\\\"Disfavored wi\",\n          \"truncated\": true\n        },\n        \"limitations\": {\n          \"text\": \"[\\\"Only seed 42 is available. Same-seed bridges are not independent repetitions; neither confidence intervals nor significance can be computed from these aggregate summaries.\\\",\\\"The 512-impression diagnostics are candidate-supplied and ordered, with 4 empty and 40 single-type cases. They are not representative population estimates or independent measurement.\\\",\\\"Attention mass and summary L2 changes do not establish event relevance, causal feature importance or a performance mechanism. Cross-checkpoint diagnostics confound retraining with the normalization.\\\",\\\"Slice interpretations are exploratory; original prospective hypotheses and exact scorer bin definitions were not supplied. Counts are reported without an invented minimum-support cutoff. Small-positive slices, including empty and pv-absen\",\n          \"truncated\": true\n        },\n        \"next_action\": {\n          \"text\": \"{\\\"action\\\":\\\"Retain baseline-din; prepare a bounded partial-correction study for a later authorized experiment phase. Do not train or modify models during this analyze phase.\\\",\\\"observation\\\":\\\"Full correction substantially hurts pooling and slightly hurts DIN, despite active diagnostic changes; the smaller DIN penalty may indicate compensation or overcorrection.\\\",\\\"mechanism_hypothesis\\\":\\\"A fixed half-strength count correction preserves useful intensity while attenuating type multiplicity, avoiding some of the penalty of full correction. Target-aware scoring may account for the attenuation of the penalty.\\\",\\\"nearest_existing_work\\\":\\\"Use the ordinary and full-corrected local factorial as the immediate controls. Search and inspect primary work on behavior-wise normalization before asserting a literature difference; no priority claim is needed for this follow-up.\\\",\\\"inherited_components\\\":\\\"Keep exist\",\n          \"truncated\": true\n        },\n        \"decision\": {\n          \"text\": \"{\\\"incumbent\\\":\\\"baseline-din\\\",\\\"promote_latest_candidate\\\":false,\\\"research_status\\\":\\\"A mechanism-distinct count-normalization candidate was successfully executed but did not improve the full-population validation objective in the supplied seed. The factorial gives provisional local evidence of interaction with attention. Further discrimination is justified; no new run is executed in this phase.\\\",\\\"scientific_maturity\\\":\\\"single-seed controlled local evidence; no repeated support or significance claim\\\"}\",\n          \"truncated\": false\n        }\n      },\n      \"proposed_updates\": [],\n      \"source_trial_refs\": [\n        \"baseline-static\",\n        \"baseline-pooled\",\n        \"baseline-din\",\n        \"r0001-ordinary_pool\",\n        \"r0001-count_corrected_pool\",\n        \"r0001-ordinary_din\",\n        \"r0001-count_corrected_din\"\n      ],\n      \"full_ref\": \"memory://agent-r0001\",\n      \"full_sha256\": \"aa37f8bb717ec2ce0978fe16468ec1cbe0db546fea8e40a58485ac8c45774b5f\",\n      \"summary_notice\": \"Bounded index view, not complete evidence. Read full_ref for original observations, alternatives and limitations. No maturity promotion is implied.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"scores\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"agent-r0008\",\n      \"knowledge_type\": \"agent\",\n      \"score\": 8.565409282572572,\n      \"indexed_tokens\": 581\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"agent-r0007\",\n      \"knowledge_type\": \"agent\",\n      \"score\": 3.8061320818588755,\n      \"indexed_tokens\": 565\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"agent-r0006\",\n      \"knowledge_type\": \"agent\",\n      \"score\": 3.1355304108543187,\n      \"indexed_tokens\": 588\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"agent-r0005\",\n      \"knowledge_type\": \"agent\",\n      \"score\": 2.958827569580298,\n      \"indexed_tokens\": 578\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"agent-r0002\",\n      \"knowledge_type\": \"agent\",\n      \"score\": 1.7773574193839365,\n      \"indexed_tokens\": 702\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"agent-r0001\",\n      \"knowledge_type\": \"agent\",\n      \"score\": 1.6792012730609251,\n      \"indexed_tokens\": 558\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
